.\--SYNOPSIS
..SYNOPSIS
..Recurring characters:
>.Shapley Morton (SM): is a large Wall Street brokerage
>.company. It has a standard pyramid shape management
>.structure. All characters, except for Roger, work for this
..company.
>.Sonny: Sonny is a good looking, well kept guy, who shaves
>.daily and wears a white shirt and a tie at all the time. As
>.a result of the lavish money in early 2000s, he never
>.developed a deep understanding of the commodity space and
>.the factors that drive it. He is using profanity liberally.
..He works for SM.
>.Roger: Roger is from Hemispheric Energy, a gas and oil
>.exploration company. He is a typical non-Wall Street
>.manager, overly positive and exaggerating. His dress style
>.is somewhat more casual as Sonny's. He has an overcomb, and
..is slightly overweight. Very shallow and vain.
>.Brett: Brett is Sonny's boss. He is a typical New England
>.WASP-y guy with a great haircut, white shirt and a tie.
>.Brett's corner office is on a high floor of SM building and
>.has great view of NY. On his desk are a photo of his wife
>.and 2 children, a model schooner. Behind the desk on the
..wall is the .  
>.Dr. Tang: Dr. Tang is a strat in the organization, I.e. he
>.works on the mathematical models. He is always referred as
>.Dr. Tang, as if he doesn't have the first name. All his
>.assistants are also Chinese, many of them with very advanced
>.PhD math/science/computer science degrees. He has a mild
>.Chinese accent, and makes grammar errors all the time, but
>.not ridiculously so. He has at least six really large
>.screens in front of him, full of spreadsheets, coding
..editors etc., and is running all sorts of analysis, coding.
>.Igor: Igor is a Russian guy from the risk management
>.department. He wears somewhat large, clumsy glasses. He
>.speaks with a deep Russian accent. He has a bad haircut (I
>.know this is cliché.) He tries to take care of his
>.appearance, but can't quite pull it all together - a large
..stain on his shirt or something always gives it away.
>.Amisha: An associate of Sonny, works underneath him. He is
>.of indian descent, very pretty - was chosen by Sonny for
>.that reason as well. Although she is very smart, she never
>.explored her smarts and pursued the carreer in finance, as
>.that is perceived noble in her family. She slowly grews
>.disillusined with not being promoted, although there is no
..reason for doing so. 
>.Joshua: Another associate of Sonny. Of Jewish descent, but
>.not religious at all. Like Amisha, he went to finance more
>.for the lack of motivation elsewhere, and doesn't really
>.like, but he is in good standing with his family because of
>.it. Tries to be helpful, but often screws things up. Quite
>.humble and submissive, and not arrogant, contrary to his
>.boss Sonny. Secretly wants to be in a more creative
..endeavours. 
..--PRELUDE
.\Sonny's Desk
>.A typical trading floor desk. Several screens with Bloomberg
>.terminals in front of him. A dispatcher phone console. Other
>.traders/sales -people around him talking on the phones,
..browsing Bloomberg, doing spreadsheet analysis.
>.Amisha and Joshua are sitting at their respective desks.
>.Joshua is trying to work on some spreadsheets, but Amisha is
>.just browsing her cell phone with only e-mail open on her
>.two screens. The camera switches between Roger, who is in an
>.office at Hemispheric, and Sonny, who is at his trading
>.desk. Sometimes the camera stays on Roger or Sonny, and the
..other's voice is heard in the background.
