..EPISODE 3: 
>.It's promotion season and both Joshua and Amisha want to
>.profit from being in a good relationship with Sonny. They
>.try it in different ways. Joshua wants to impress him with
>.his spreadsheet skills and being early/late in the office.
>.Amisha flirts with him and is overly nice. At the end, none
>.of them gets promotion, as Brett does not see anything that
>.Amisha and Joshua have done - Sonny took all of their work
>.for himself. This creates extra tension during the holiday
..season. 
..EPISODE 4: 
>.During the regulator season the large banks need to conduct
>.stress tests. Igor discovered that there is a big error in
>.the risk computation system and that Sonny's desk would be
>.affected and with it Sonny's bonus. That creates tension and
>.a lot of angry words between the risk department and the
>.desk. At the end they resolve the issue. Sonny's bonus is
..very affected and he contemplates leaving. 
..EPISODE 5: 
>.On the account of not getting the promotion, and some lax
>.language by Sonny in the meetings, Joshua leaves and files a
>.lawsuit agains SM for discrimination. The lawsuit is large
>.and Sonny and Brett are both pissed that in addition to bad
>.publicity, their bonuses will be affected. Brett comes with
>.an idea of having his department participate in a seminar
..about ethics, morality and office relationships. 
..EPISODE 6: 
>.After a few more deals go through Sonny's appetite increases
>.and he wants to upend Brett. But knowing that Dr. Tang and
>.Igor are not his best friends, he tries to isolate them in
..the promotion process with respect to his boss.
..EPISODE 7: 
>.The business is downsizing and there will be people fired.
>.Sonny's position is threatened as he wanted to push Brett
>.out but he also has to decide who of the two subordinates he
..is going to fire. 
